      "rationale": "Directly captures a core review theme with a graded quality scale useful for group comparison across sentiment. Values track the text soundly (good pizza -> good_solid; service-only complaint review -> not_present)."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_praised_highlight",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.72,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a finer axis of what specifically is praised, giving some new leverage, but overlaps substantially with food_quality_signal for the positive cases (largely redundant when food is 'excellent'). Values are grounded (specific dish highlighted in the pita and pizza reviews)."
    },
    {
      "name": "atmosphere_ambiance_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A distinct thematic dimension useful for the sentiment comparison. Mostly 'not_present', which is appropriate silence for these rows, and no invented ambiance claims observed in the samples."
    },
    {
      "name": "return_recommend_intent",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Behavioral-intent axis that correlates with and enriches sentiment analysis. Grounded on explicit cues (warn_others for cabana, return_no for worst-service). 'explicit_return_yes' for YLP-0001 is a mild inference (strong loyalty language but no literal 'I'll return' statement), and 'conditional_return' for YLP-0003 is a loose but defensible read of the 'maybe if they offer' line."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.88,
  "source_groundedness": 0.91,
  "rationale": "The added columns decompose reviews into genuine thematic axes (service, food quality, food highlights, atmosphere, return intent) that directly support comparing themes across positive and negative Yelp sentiment. Each offers a real grouping/comparison dimension; only food_praised_highlight partially overlaps food_quality_signal, slightly reducing its independent leverage. Values are sound readings of the source text with appropriate 'not_present' for silent rows; a few intent/mixed labels are mild inferences but remain defensible, and no clear hallucinations were observed."
